	<p>
		I am a <strong>Senior Customer Engineer at Google Cloud</strong> based in Austin, Texas.
		My professional focus centers on enterprise artificial intelligence, modern application architecture, and multi-model agentic workflows.
	</p>

	<h2>Enterprise AI & Multi-Model Architecture</h2>
	<p>
		In enterprise computing, no single model solves every business challenge. I work daily with Fortune 500 customers to design and build production AI systems that balance:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Latency & Throughput</strong>: Choosing the right model tier for real-time customer interactions.</li>
		<li><strong>Cost & Token Economics</strong>: Leveraging prompt caching, prefix optimization, and compact system designs.</li>
		<li><strong>Modality & Context Fit</strong>: Harnessing Google's massive context windows and multimodal Gemini models alongside specialized tool-calling models like Claude over Model Context Protocol (MCP).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Homelab & Production Engineering</h2>
	<p>
		I strongly believe that the best architects are active builders. Outside of client advisory, I maintain an enterprise-grade multi-host homelab (running Proxmox VE, OPNsense firewalls, TrueNAS, Home Assistant, and autonomous agent supervisors) where I test new architectures, protocol standards, and automation pipelines under real operational conditions.
	</p>

